error[E0277]: `UnattestedGuard` does not check HTTP requests
  --> tests/integration/diagnostics/unattested_guard_on_a_controller.rs:21:14
   |
21 | #[use_guards(UnattestedGuard)]
   |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this guard has no `check_http`
   |
help: the trait `HttpGuard` is not implemented for `UnattestedGuard`
  --> tests/integration/diagnostics/unattested_guard_on_a_controller.rs:14:1
   |
14 | struct UnattestedGuard;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: a guard bound on a `#[controller]` / `#[routes]`, or on a `#[gateway]` struct (whose guards run on the upgrade, an HTTP `GET`), runs `Guard::check_http` — whose default is `Ok(())`, so binding one that does not override it passes every request silently
   = note: override `check_http`, then declare `impl HttpGuard for UnattestedGuard {}`; or bind this guard at the edge it does check — a `#[resolver]` (`GraphqlGuard`), beside a `#[subscribe_message]` (`WsGuard`, per message rather than at the upgrade), or an `#[mcp]` host (`McpGuard`)
note: required by a bound in `__nestrs_assert_guard_capability`
  --> tests/integration/diagnostics/unattested_guard_on_a_controller.rs:20:1
   |
20 | #[controller(path = "/demo")]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `__nestrs_assert_guard_capability`
21 | #[use_guards(UnattestedGuard)]
   |              --------------- required by a bound in this function
   = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `controller` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
